:question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-7b216cfc-dcbe-5847-9bef-9747d27351d3" :answer/id #uuid "7b216cfc-dcbe-5847-9bef-9747d27351d3"] ["answer-7b216cfc-dcbe-5847-9bef-9747d27351d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7b216cfc-dcbe-5847-9bef-9747d27351d3" :answer/value "\\pm 49"] [17592186175036 :answer-field/correct 17592186175040] [17592186175036 :answer-field/choices "answer-7b216cfc-dcbe-5847-9bef-9747d27351d3"] ["question-15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547" :question/id #uuid "15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547"] ["question-15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547" :question/math-academy-id "q-103627"] ["question-15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547" :question/problem "$\\frac{2x-3y+8z}{6}=$"] ["question-15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547" :question/worked-solution "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-3y+8z}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{2x}{6}-\\frac{3y}{6}+\\frac{8z}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{6}\\cdot x-\\frac{3}{6}\\cdot y+\\frac{8}{6}\\cdot z & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot y+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot z & = \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{y}{2}+\\frac{4z}{3} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb"] ["answer-8ae6efe2-2a69-5edd-a91a-e313b3c19515" :answer/id #uuid "8ae6efe2-2a69-5edd-a91a-e313b3c19515"] ["answer-8ae6efe2-2a69-5edd-a91a-e313b3c19515" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8ae6efe2-2a69-5edd-a91a-e313b3c19515" :answer/value "2x-3y+4z"] ["answer-b90bf318-c0cb-58e1-9f0f-37146557bef8" :answer/id #uuid "b90bf318-c0cb-58e1-9f0f-37146557bef8"] ["answer-b90bf318-c0cb-58e1-9f0f-37146557bef8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b90bf318-c0cb-58e1-9f0f-37146557bef8" :answer/value "3x-2y+\\frac{4z}{3}"] ["answer-154b90d1-09df-5975-9106-7abfa155a7f3" :answer/id #uuid "154b90d1-09df-5975-9106-7abfa155a7f3"] ["answer-154b90d1-09df-5975-9106-7abfa155a7f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-154b90d1-09df-5975-9106-7abfa155a7f3" :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-2y+4z"] ["answer-77da7769-a1d4-5c71-8686-24a20677c965" :answer/id #uuid "77da7769-a1d4-5c71-8686-24a20677c965"] ["answer-77da7769-a1d4-5c71-8686-24a20677c965" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77da7769-a1d4-5c71-8686-24a20677c965" :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{y}{2}+\\frac{4z}{3}"] ["answer-8274a2c9-bf10-549e-8286-c1d9ea4ef1c0" :answer/id #uuid "8274a2c9-bf10-549e-8286-c1d9ea4ef1c0"] ["answer-8274a2c9-bf10-549e-8286-c1d9ea4ef1c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8274a2c9-bf10-549e-8286-c1d9ea4ef1c0" :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}-y-\\frac{4z}{3}"] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/correct "answer-77da7769-a1d4-5c71-8686-24a20677c965"] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/choices "answer-8ae6efe2-2a69-5edd-a91a-e313b3c19515"] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/choices "answer-b90bf318-c0cb-58e1-9f0f-37146557bef8"] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/choices "answer-154b90d1-09df-5975-9106-7abfa155a7f3"] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/choices "answer-77da7769-a1d4-5c71-8686-24a20677c965"] ["answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb" :answer-field/choices "answer-8274a2c9-bf10-549e-8286-c1d9ea4ef1c0"] ["question-15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-beaa49a3-09ca-5bd9-8b13-bb052a6be6fb"] [17592186064258 :knowledge-point/questions "question-15a43dbb-9c91-5be9-a586-59bfd5235547"] ["question-f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e" :question/id #uuid "f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e"] ["question-f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-162057"] ["question-f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e" :question/problem "$(-5)÷4$ is equivalent to"] ["question-f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e" :question/worked-solution "Here, we are dividing a negative number $(-5)$ by a positive one $(4).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-5)÷4=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n5÷4=1\\,\\text{R}\\,1=1\\,\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-5)÷4=-1\\,\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$"] ["question-f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/id #uuid "30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27"] ["answer-057d7c6e-29e6-5051-a5e8-b0998b5d0542" :answer/id #uuid "057d7c6e-29e6-5051-a5e8-b0998b5d0542"] ["answer-057d7c6e-29e6-5051-a5e8-b0998b5d0542" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-057d7c6e-29e6-5051-a5e8-b0998b5d0542" :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-2e6041d2-fb6a-5f6a-8e9c-714854eda1d9" :answer/id #uuid "2e6041d2-fb6a-5f6a-8e9c-714854eda1d9"] ["answer-2e6041d2-fb6a-5f6a-8e9c-714854eda1d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2e6041d2-fb6a-5f6a-8e9c-714854eda1d9" :answer/value "-1\\,\\frac{3}{4}"] ["answer-f19ae37e-0dc6-5e4e-b694-e737cfd667d3" :answer/id #uuid "f19ae37e-0dc6-5e4e-b694-e737cfd667d3"] ["answer-f19ae37e-0dc6-5e4e-b694-e737cfd667d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f19ae37e-0dc6-5e4e-b694-e737cfd667d3" :answer/value "-2\\,\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-2b653396-bc27-5145-b8ac-e1022471deab" :answer/id #uuid "2b653396-bc27-5145-b8ac-e1022471deab"] ["answer-2b653396-bc27-5145-b8ac-e1022471deab" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2b653396-bc27-5145-b8ac-e1022471deab" :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-76d979a8-8760-59e0-812f-a0b817c69f44" :answer/id #uuid "76d979a8-8760-59e0-812f-a0b817c69f44"] ["answer-76d979a8-8760-59e0-812f-a0b817c69f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-76d979a8-8760-59e0-812f-a0b817c69f44" :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/correct "answer-057d7c6e-29e6-5051-a5e8-b0998b5d0542"] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/choices "answer-057d7c6e-29e6-5051-a5e8-b0998b5d0542"] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/choices "answer-2e6041d2-fb6a-5f6a-8e9c-714854eda1d9"] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/choices "answer-f19ae37e-0dc6-5e4e-b694-e737cfd667d3"] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/choices "answer-2b653396-bc27-5145-b8ac-e1022471deab"] ["answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27" :answer-field/choices "answer-76d979a8-8760-59e0-812f-a0b817c69f44"] ["question-f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-30c3593c-4e14-5e97-8e53-48b988006b27"] [17592186198382 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f462c87b-3e02-54b6-b206-e6def06b7c2e"] ["question-dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd" :question/id #uuid "dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd"] ["question-dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-141915"] ["question-dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd" :question/problem "$(-5)(2x+3y)-5y=$"] ["question-dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd" :question/worked-solution "First, we distribute the $(-5)$ over each of the terms in parentheses.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}(-5)(2x+3y)-5y & = \\\\ (-5)\\cdot 2x+(-5)\\cdot 3y-5y & = \\\\ (-10x)+(-15y)-5y & = \\\\ -10x-15y-5y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we collect like terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}-10x-15y-5y & = \\\\ -10x+(-15y-5y) & = \\\\ -10x-20y\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/id #uuid "add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f"] ["answer-d17a4b4a-c1a9-581c-8038-8ac220d502da" :answer/id #uuid "d17a4b4a-c1a9-581c-8038-8ac220d502da"] ["answer-d17a4b4a-c1a9-581c-8038-8ac220d502da" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d17a4b4a-c1a9-581c-8038-8ac220d502da" :answer/value "-10x+15y"] ["answer-9183e516-17fb-5257-9c76-19c9409e87ff" :answer/id #uuid "9183e516-17fb-5257-9c76-19c9409e87ff"] ["answer-9183e516-17fb-5257-9c76-19c9409e87ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9183e516-17fb-5257-9c76-19c9409e87ff" :answer/value "-10x-20y"] ["answer-5ae20b64-ab72-5509-bc96-2ab8d1fafe50" :answer/id #uuid "5ae20b64-ab72-5509-bc96-2ab8d1fafe50"] ["answer-5ae20b64-ab72-5509-bc96-2ab8d1fafe50" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5ae20b64-ab72-5509-bc96-2ab8d1fafe50" :answer/value "-15x-15y"] ["answer-272cdf46-670b-5698-b4dd-e9cb21841355" :answer/id #uuid "272cdf46-670b-5698-b4dd-e9cb21841355"] ["answer-272cdf46-670b-5698-b4dd-e9cb21841355" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-272cdf46-670b-5698-b4dd-e9cb21841355" :answer/value "10x-8y"] ["answer-2147df49-a826-5ebb-a3dc-ebe444239e0f" :answer/id #uuid "2147df49-a826-5ebb-a3dc-ebe444239e0f"] ["answer-2147df49-a826-5ebb-a3dc-ebe444239e0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2147df49-a826-5ebb-a3dc-ebe444239e0f" :answer/value "2x-20y"] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/correct "answer-9183e516-17fb-5257-9c76-19c9409e87ff"] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/choices "answer-d17a4b4a-c1a9-581c-8038-8ac220d502da"] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/choices "answer-9183e516-17fb-5257-9c76-19c9409e87ff"] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/choices "answer-5ae20b64-ab72-5509-bc96-2ab8d1fafe50"] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/choices "answer-272cdf46-670b-5698-b4dd-e9cb21841355"] ["answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f" :answer-field/choices "answer-2147df49-a826-5ebb-a3dc-ebe444239e0f"] ["question-dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-add26c3a-8ea0-579d-b7c2-eb977845c92f"] [17592186054786 :knowledge-point/questions "question-dcca9682-5c6e-581c-bcc3-60c96a3dddcd"] [17592186138776 :question/worked-solution "The red segment contains all values between  $-2$ and $1.$ In addition,\n\n- the open circle at $-2$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $-2,$ while\n\n- the open circle at $1$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $1.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $-2<x<1.$"] [17592186138776 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-4592c636-8f62-592d-9c3e-276e70810db5" :answer/id #uuid "4592c636-8f62-592d-9c3e-276e70810db5"] ["answer-4592c636-8f62-592d-9c3e-276e70810db5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4592c636-8f62-592d-9c3e-276e70810db5" :answer/value "-2<x<1"] ["answer-9871d376-12ef-5e6e-af44-fe57744b0653" :answer/id #uuid "9871d376-12ef-5e6e-af44-fe57744b0653"] ["answer-9871d376-12ef-5e6e-af44-fe57744b0653" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9871d376-12ef-5e6e-af44-fe57744b0653" :answer/value "-2<x\\le 2"] ["answer-9be6b73e-0418-56db-90da-473d702f855a" :answer/id #uuid "9be6b73e-0418-56db-90da-473d702f855a"] ["answer-9be6b73e-0418-56db-90da-473d702f855a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9be6b73e-0418-56db-90da-473d702f855a" :answer/value "-2\\le x<1"] ["answer-ef9054fd-d157-5ca3-9428-0aa2e99411c5" :answer/id #uuid "ef9054fd-d157-5ca3-9428-0aa2e99411c5"] ["answer-ef9054fd-d157-5ca3-9428-0aa2e99411c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ef9054fd-d157-5ca3-9428-0aa2e99411c5" :answer/value "-2\\le x\\le 1"] ["answer-14295dff-21db-5fe1-a96c-8930ed638809" :answer/id #uuid "14295dff-21db-5fe1-a96c-8930ed638809"] ["answer-14295dff-21db-5fe1-a96c-8930ed638809" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-14295dff-21db-5fe1-a96c-8930ed638809" :answer/value "$x<-2$ or $x\\ge 1$"] [17592186135604 :answer-field/correct "answer-4592c636-8f62-592d-9c3e-276e70810db5"] [17592186135604 :answer-field/choices "answer-4592c636-8f62-592d-9c3e-276e70810db5"] [17592186135604 :answer-field/choices "answer-9871d376-12ef-5e6e-af44-fe57744b0653"] [17592186135604 :answer-field/choices "answer-9be6b73e-0418-56db-90da-473d702f855a"] [17592186135604 :answer-field/choices "answer-ef9054fd-d157-5ca3-9428-0aa2e99411c5"] [17592186135604 :answer-field/choices "answer-14295dff-21db-5fe1-a96c-8930ed638809"] ["question-f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3" :question/id #uuid "f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3"] ["question-f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-155053"] ["question-f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a31a793df705b6cbe8dddb648ca6a0d2ebb6f4eb724ff8b99682f48cafb072a0.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams above shows three collinear points?"] ["question-f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3" :question/worked-solution "Three (or more) points are collinear if a straight line passes through all points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our diagrams in turn.\n\n- Diagram I shows three points that are *not* collinear. We can't draw a straight line that passes through all three points.\n\n![](images/aa/aad13ab456bc61c90522725ddb60f481c6138a9e53a50136d691ddd344349cf1.png)\n\n- Diagram II shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/14/143e831321a485a0e57b706c6df89273bd92b3134d691d1ef41a67b7f7076481.png)\n\n- Diagram III shows three collinear points. There is a straight line that passes through all three of these points.\n\n![](images/2c/2c361eea2a598de063dc62375716ca5bdb7b0a06d4c30cf9a5c420cd9cc48e4b.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""] ["question-f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0"] ["answer-a0af0a69-97d7-566d-ae7c-64e83031da5e" :answer/id #uuid "a0af0a69-97d7-566d-ae7c-64e83031da5e"] ["answer-a0af0a69-97d7-566d-ae7c-64e83031da5e" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a0af0a69-97d7-566d-ae7c-64e83031da5e" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-ea8c32c2-3154-5e95-ba13-18e6ee28fe41" :answer/id #uuid "ea8c32c2-3154-5e95-ba13-18e6ee28fe41"] ["answer-ea8c32c2-3154-5e95-ba13-18e6ee28fe41" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-ea8c32c2-3154-5e95-ba13-18e6ee28fe41" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-56e1f971-d113-5022-8210-b1ab22042601" :answer/id #uuid "56e1f971-d113-5022-8210-b1ab22042601"] ["answer-56e1f971-d113-5022-8210-b1ab22042601" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-56e1f971-d113-5022-8210-b1ab22042601" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-20256647-65f2-5046-a78f-8335ba715a35" :answer/id #uuid "20256647-65f2-5046-a78f-8335ba715a35"] ["answer-20256647-65f2-5046-a78f-8335ba715a35" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-20256647-65f2-5046-a78f-8335ba715a35" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-1643603d-c5ae-57d3-9136-823babe8d447" :answer/id #uuid "1643603d-c5ae-57d3-9136-823babe8d447"] ["answer-1643603d-c5ae-57d3-9136-823babe8d447" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-1643603d-c5ae-57d3-9136-823babe8d447" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/correct "answer-56e1f971-d113-5022-8210-b1ab22042601"] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/choices "answer-a0af0a69-97d7-566d-ae7c-64e83031da5e"] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/choices "answer-ea8c32c2-3154-5e95-ba13-18e6ee28fe41"] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/choices "answer-56e1f971-d113-5022-8210-b1ab22042601"] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/choices "answer-20256647-65f2-5046-a78f-8335ba715a35"] ["answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0" :answer-field/choices "answer-1643603d-c5ae-57d3-9136-823babe8d447"] ["question-f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-7892cfad-b772-5810-a92d-5b07af0c75e0"] [17592186110675 :knowledge-point/questions "question-f8c7f0d6-8dc6-549e-8375-7c33cf7277e3"] ["question-553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b" :question/id #uuid "553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b"] ["question-553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60651"] ["question-553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b" :question/problem "![](images/c9/c9b42a179625b667cb54f1b597127809d851a1b7a830a2632b09402ecb790330.png)\n\nWhat is the distance between the points $(3,2)$  and $(-2,2)?$"] ["question-553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $5$ units, so the distance equals $5.$\n\n![](images/49/498674b4a4667b57be1574a081bbb948350754ed8993c14428ad8f31ee17bd90.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/f3/f3811804824e802c4cb20af85bac7f21f6c4e0f60e0430607c876e1cf27b7cd3.png)\n\nThe point $(-2,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(3,2)$ is at a distance of $3$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $2+3=5.$"] ["question-553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/id #uuid "b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d"] ["answer-07de2851-2484-55be-a23c-13409d875b06" :answer/id #uuid "07de2851-2484-55be-a23c-13409d875b06"] ["answer-07de2851-2484-55be-a23c-13409d875b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-07de2851-2484-55be-a23c-13409d875b06" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-f8f314d3-fb52-56ee-b641-75480fce47ce" :answer/id #uuid "f8f314d3-fb52-56ee-b641-75480fce47ce"] ["answer-f8f314d3-fb52-56ee-b641-75480fce47ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f8f314d3-fb52-56ee-b641-75480fce47ce" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-fac4f137-1d76-5d07-8f85-2cdd7cfafb4d" :answer/id #uuid "fac4f137-1d76-5d07-8f85-2cdd7cfafb4d"] ["answer-fac4f137-1d76-5d07-8f85-2cdd7cfafb4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fac4f137-1d76-5d07-8f85-2cdd7cfafb4d" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-c7bc695b-36dc-5765-94b9-c570c3a39720" :answer/id #uuid "c7bc695b-36dc-5765-94b9-c570c3a39720"] ["answer-c7bc695b-36dc-5765-94b9-c570c3a39720" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c7bc695b-36dc-5765-94b9-c570c3a39720" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7" :answer/id #uuid "bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7"] ["answer-bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/correct "answer-bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7"] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/choices "answer-07de2851-2484-55be-a23c-13409d875b06"] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/choices "answer-f8f314d3-fb52-56ee-b641-75480fce47ce"] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/choices "answer-fac4f137-1d76-5d07-8f85-2cdd7cfafb4d"] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/choices "answer-c7bc695b-36dc-5765-94b9-c570c3a39720"] ["answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/choices "answer-bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7"] ["question-553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d"] [17592186073900 :knowledge-point/questions "question-553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b"] ["question-aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e" :question/id #uuid "aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e"] ["question-aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-93027"] ["question-aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e" :question/problem "A water tank with a capacity of $5,000$ liters is filled with water to $42.5%$ of its capacity. How much water is in the tank?"] ["question-aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the capacity of the tank, which is $5,000$ liters. The percentage is $42.5%,$ and the part is the amount of water in the tank.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n42.5%=42.5÷100=0.425\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =42.5%\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =0.425\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =2,125\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $42.5%$ of $5,000$ is $2,125.$ Thus, there are $2,125$ liters of water in the tank.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n42.5%=\\frac{42.5}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =42.5%\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =\\frac{42.5}{100}\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =42.5\\times \\frac{5,000}{100} \\\\  & =42.5\\times 50 \\\\  & =2,125\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $42.5%$ of $5,000$ is $2,125.$ Thus, there are $2,125$ liters of water in the tank."] ["question-aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc"] ["answer-2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358" :answer/id #uuid "2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358"] ["answer-2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358" :answer/value "$2,125$ liters"] ["answer-3ed97be4-c5cb-5b26-8151-563b09ffe246" :answer/id #uuid "3ed97be4-c5cb-5b26-8151-563b09ffe246"] ["answer-3ed97be4-c5cb-5b26-8151-563b09ffe246" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3ed97be4-c5cb-5b26-8151-563b09ffe246" :answer/value "$2,225$ liters"] ["answer-daa496f1-eb97-5c4e-bcee-4319394a7cda" :answer/id #uuid "daa496f1-eb97-5c4e-bcee-4319394a7cda"] ["answer-daa496f1-eb97-5c4e-bcee-4319394a7cda" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-daa496f1-eb97-5c4e-bcee-4319394a7cda" :answer/value "$2,250$ liters"] ["answer-4fb0f9be-d361-51b6-99a5-14990f65e490" :answer/id #uuid "4fb0f9be-d361-51b6-99a5-14990f65e490"] ["answer-4fb0f9be-d361-51b6-99a5-14990f65e490" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4fb0f9be-d361-51b6-99a5-14990f65e490" :answer/value "$3,125$ liters"] ["answer-4140294a-4de5-516e-a556-10df8fbe6d5d" :answer/id #uuid "4140294a-4de5-516e-a556-10df8fbe6d5d"] ["answer-4140294a-4de5-516e-a556-10df8fbe6d5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4140294a-4de5-516e-a556-10df8fbe6d5d" :answer/value "$3,250$ liters"] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/correct "answer-2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358"] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/choices "answer-2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358"] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/choices "answer-3ed97be4-c5cb-5b26-8151-563b09ffe246"] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/choices "answer-daa496f1-eb97-5c4e-bcee-4319394a7cda"] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/choices "answer-4fb0f9be-d361-51b6-99a5-14990f65e490"] ["answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/choices "answer-4140294a-4de5-516e-a556-10df8fbe6d5d"] ["question-aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc"] [17592186147594 :knowledge-point/questions "question-aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e"] ["question-42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1" :question/id #uuid "42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1"] ["question-42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-101566"] ["question-42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1" :question/problem "What number can be added to $-35$ to get a sum of $0?$"] ["question-42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1" :question/worked-solution "The number that can be added to $-35$ to give $0$ is the additive inverse of $-35.$\n\nTo find the additive inverse of the number $-35$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain\n\n$$\n-\\,(-35)=35.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-35)+35=-35+35=0\\,✓\n$$"] ["question-42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5"] ["answer-0c2d8b23-480d-58a0-a53f-2e077ed9eded" :answer/id #uuid "0c2d8b23-480d-58a0-a53f-2e077ed9eded"] ["answer-0c2d8b23-480d-58a0-a53f-2e077ed9eded" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0c2d8b23-480d-58a0-a53f-2e077ed9eded" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{15}"] ["answer-8dcff317-0a65-5de1-9449-fd4587a618e0" :answer/id #uuid "8dcff317-0a65-5de1-9449-fd4587a618e0"] ["answer-8dcff317-0a65-5de1-9449-fd4587a618e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8dcff317-0a65-5de1-9449-fd4587a618e0" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{35}"] ["answer-1ebe73ea-6758-5ea6-a455-730e9fbe8545" :answer/id #uuid "1ebe73ea-6758-5ea6-a455-730e9fbe8545"] ["answer-1ebe73ea-6758-5ea6-a455-730e9fbe8545" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1ebe73ea-6758-5ea6-a455-730e9fbe8545" :answer/value "15"] ["answer-eacbba2a-ca7e-5120-b5aa-f3d6d4b09848" :answer/id #uuid "eacbba2a-ca7e-5120-b5aa-f3d6d4b09848"] ["answer-eacbba2a-ca7e-5120-b5aa-f3d6d4b09848" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eacbba2a-ca7e-5120-b5aa-f3d6d4b09848" :answer/value "35"] ["answer-8390a06a-40ab-56b4-bf37-2cc84dc97a79" :answer/id #uuid "8390a06a-40ab-56b4-bf37-2cc84dc97a79"] ["answer-8390a06a-40ab-56b4-bf37-2cc84dc97a79" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8390a06a-40ab-56b4-bf37-2cc84dc97a79" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}"] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/correct "answer-eacbba2a-ca7e-5120-b5aa-f3d6d4b09848"] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/choices "answer-0c2d8b23-480d-58a0-a53f-2e077ed9eded"] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/choices "answer-8dcff317-0a65-5de1-9449-fd4587a618e0"] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/choices "answer-1ebe73ea-6758-5ea6-a455-730e9fbe8545"] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/choices "answer-eacbba2a-ca7e-5120-b5aa-f3d6d4b09848"] ["answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5" :answer-field/choices "answer-8390a06a-40ab-56b4-bf37-2cc84dc97a79"] ["question-42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-672bb081-9c15-5ea5-a6d5-d6d4d17fafa5"] [17592186073821 :knowledge-point/questions "question-42762342-58bc-5c22-b022-fb45988d86d1"] [17592186106387 :question/problem "![](images/14/14b60e420cd071378f0b6a6f4c23891779733ae648d667f910617da9341aa9e4.png)\n\nWhich sides are consecutive to $\\overset{―}{DE}?$"] [17592186106387 :question/worked-solution "Two sides are consecutive if they have a vertex in common. Therefore, $\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$ are consecutive sides to $\\overset{―}{DE}.$"] [17592186106387 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194" :answer/id #uuid "efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194"] ["answer-efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194" :answer/value "\\overset{―}{AB}"] ["answer-87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135" :answer/id #uuid "87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135"] ["answer-87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135" :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AF}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$"] ["answer-1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec" :answer/id #uuid "1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec"] ["answer-1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec" :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$"] ["answer-a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381" :answer/id #uuid "a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381"] ["answer-a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381" :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$"] ["answer-5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b" :answer/id #uuid "5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b"] ["answer-5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b" :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{EF}$ and $\\overset{―}{AF}$"] [17592186104470 :answer-field/correct "answer-a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381"] [17592186104470 :answer-field/choices "answer-efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194"] [17592186104470 :answer-field/choices "answer-87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135"] [17592186104470 :answer-field/choices "answer-1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec"] [17592186104470 :answer-field/choices "answer-a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381"] [17592186104470 :answer-field/choices "answer-5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b"] ["question-4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0" :question/id #uuid "4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0"] ["question-4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-101460"] ["question-4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0" :question/problem "![](images/de/de806ae4a790c7339d49e362204a7a16257a3cb43165e0992f9a35afffed01bd.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of triangles to hexagons is $1:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there is $1$ triangle for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ hexagons."] ["question-4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0" :question/worked-solution "First, we count the number of triangles. We see that there are $2$ triangles.\n\nThen, we count the number of hexagons. We see that there are $10$ hexagons.\n\nSo the ratio of triangles to hexagons is $2:10.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,2 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,10 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,5 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that $1:5$ is equivalent to $2:10.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of triangles to hexagons is $1:5$ because there is $1$ triangle for every $5$ hexagons.\""] ["question-4b671a86-bc70-5855-bc03-8c1fbe9580d0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["ans